# T-1042: ADT constructor type mismatch — comparing variants of different tags.
# The type checker detects when two nominal variants from the same type have different tags
# and emits "cannot unify nominal variants with different tags".
# Evaluation proceeds (type errors are advisory) — [= Ok Error] returns Bool(false)
# because the variants have different tags at runtime.
[
  Result: [type Ok Error]
  ok-val:  Ok
  err-val: Error
  mismatch: [= ok-val err-val]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Variant(Result.Ok, Null), "Error": Variant(Result.Error, Null)}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Null), "err-val": Variant(Result.Error, Null), "mismatch": Bool(false)})

=== warn
[UnificationFailure] cannot unify Error with String
